content.text:
I’ve narrowed the per-repo design to three testable contracts before implementation:

- only successfully adopted repos are replay targets;
- replay is recursion-safe and receives the untouched original hook payload;
- token usage is retained only by the selected primary replay (the parent keeps it only when the current repo is primary).

I’m writing those wiring tests first so the subprocess fan-out can’t accidentally multiply evidence or token totals.

