content.text:
The hook-install audit is clean:

- installs take a cross-process flock in the Git common dir, so all worktrees serialize on one lock;
- uninstall takes the same lock, preventing install/remove races;
- existing user hooks are moved to `.pre-entire` only while holding that lock;
- replacement hook files are published atomically.

So I would not add code merely to game the 80 risk score. That score is measuring consequence/blast radius, which remains high because this is the now-combined global feature. The probability-oriented signals are healthier: security found no exploit, confidence rose to 83, every GitHub check is green, and there are still zero open findings. Only the Entire gate runner remains pending.

